  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 403.03 Distribution Piping Materials Inventory",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 403.03 Distribution Piping Materials Inventory.\n\n(a) The owner or operator (O/O) of a community water system (CWS) shall identify and report to the department whether the following construction materials are present in the distribution system of the CWS:\n\n(1) Lead from piping, solder, caulking, interior lining of distribution mains, alloys, and home plumbing;\n\n(2) Copper from piping and alloys, service lines, and home plumbing;\n\n(3) Galvanized piping, service lines, and home plumbing;\n\n(4) Ferrous piping materials such as cast iron and steel; and\n\n(5) Asbestos cement pipe.\n\n(b) The O/O shall maintain and update as necessary a lead service line inventory and lead service line replacement plan meeting the requirements of 40 CFR 141 Subpart I, 7-1-24 edition.\n\nSource. #12181, eff 5-23-17; ss by #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
